Feature: Therapeutic Area Study Aggregation Analysis

  This feature aggregates study data from the Unity Catalog table "purgo_playground.study_therapeutic_analysis" to provide insights into study progress and effectiveness across therapeutic areas. The analysis groups data by "therapeutic_area" and calculates total studies, completed studies, ongoing studies, and average enrolled subjects per therapeutic area.

  Background:
    Given the Unity Catalog is "purgo_databricks"
    And the schema is "purgo_playground"
    And the source table is "study_therapeutic_analysis"
    And the table contains columns: "therapeutic_area" (string), "study_title" (string), "study_conduct_status" (string), "enrolled_subjects" (integer)

  # Happy Path: Valid data, all required fields present
  Scenario: Aggregate study metrics per therapeutic area with valid data
    Given the table "study_therapeutic_analysis" contains valid records for all required columns
    When the data is grouped by "therapeutic_area"
    Then the output should include columns: "therapeutic_area", "total_studies", "completed_studies", "ongoing_studies", "avg_enrolled_subjects"
    And "total_studies" is the count of all studies per "therapeutic_area"
    And "completed_studies" is the count of studies where "study_conduct_status" = "Completed" per "therapeutic_area"
    And "ongoing_studies" is the count of studies where "study_conduct_status" = "Ongoing" per "therapeutic_area"
    And "avg_enrolled_subjects" is the average of "enrolled_subjects" per "therapeutic_area"
    And all numeric columns are integers except "avg_enrolled_subjects", which is a float with 2 decimal places

  # Error Scenario: Missing required columns
  Scenario Outline: Error when required columns are missing
    Given the table "study_therapeutic_analysis" is missing the column "<missing_column>"
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then an error should be raised with message "Column <missing_column> not found in source table"

    Examples:
      | missing_column        |
      | therapeutic_area      |
      | study_conduct_status  |
      | enrolled_subjects     |

  # Error Scenario: Null or invalid values in key columns
  Scenario Outline: Handle null or invalid values in key columns
    Given a record in "study_therapeutic_analysis" where "<column>" is <value>
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the record should be excluded from all aggregations
    And a warning should be logged: "Excluded record with null or invalid <column>"

    Examples:
      | column              | value   |
      | therapeutic_area    | null    |
      | study_conduct_status| null    |
      | enrolled_subjects   | null    |
      | enrolled_subjects   | -1      |

  # Error Scenario: Invalid study_conduct_status values
  Scenario Outline: Handle unexpected study_conduct_status values
    Given a record in "study_therapeutic_analysis" where "study_conduct_status" = "<status>"
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the record should be included in "total_studies" count
    And the record should not be included in "completed_studies" or "ongoing_studies"
    And a warning should be logged: "Unrecognized study_conduct_status: <status>"

    Examples:
      | status      |
      | Terminated  |
      | Withdrawn   |
      | Suspended   |
      | null        |

  # Data-driven: Multiple therapeutic areas and study statuses
  Scenario Outline: Aggregation for multiple therapeutic areas and statuses
    Given the table "study_therapeutic_analysis" contains the following records:
      | therapeutic_area | study_title      | study_conduct_status | enrolled_subjects |
      | <area>           | <title1>         | <status1>           | <subjects1>      |
      | <area>           | <title2>         | <status2>           | <subjects2>      |
      | <area>           | <title3>         | <status3>           | <subjects3>      |
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the output for "<area>" should be:
      | therapeutic_area | total_studies | completed_studies | ongoing_studies | avg_enrolled_subjects |
      | <area>           | <total>       | <completed>       | <ongoing>       | <avg>                 |

    Examples:
      | area         | title1         | status1    | subjects1 | title2         | status2    | subjects2 | title3         | status3    | subjects3 | total | completed | ongoing | avg  |
      | Cardiology   | Study A        | Completed  | 100       | Study B        | Ongoing    | 150       | Study C        | Completed  | 200       | 3     | 2         | 1      | 150.0|
      | Oncology     | Study D        | Ongoing    | 80        | Study E        | Ongoing    | 120       | Study F        | Withdrawn  | 90        | 3     | 0         | 2      | 96.7 |
      | Neurology    | Study G        | Completed  | 50        | Study H        | Terminated | 60        | Study I        | Completed  | 70        | 3     | 2         | 0      | 60.0 |

  # Validation: Output column formats and ordering
  Scenario: Validate output column formats and ordering
    Given the aggregation logic has executed successfully
    When the output is generated
    Then the columns should be ordered as: "therapeutic_area", "total_studies", "completed_studies", "ongoing_studies", "avg_enrolled_subjects"
    And "therapeutic_area" is a string
    And "total_studies", "completed_studies", "ongoing_studies" are integers
    And "avg_enrolled_subjects" is a float with 2 decimal places

  # Validation: No studies for a therapeutic area
  Scenario: Therapeutic area with no studies
    Given "study_therapeutic_analysis" contains no records for "therapeutic_area" = "Immunology"
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then "Immunology" should not appear in the output

  # Validation: Duplicate study titles within a therapeutic area
  Scenario: Duplicate study titles within a therapeutic area
    Given "study_therapeutic_analysis" contains multiple records with the same "study_title" under one "therapeutic_area"
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then each record should be counted separately in "total_studies"
    And aggregation should not deduplicate by "study_title"

  # Validation: Handling of zero enrolled subjects
  Scenario: Studies with zero enrolled subjects
    Given a record in "study_therapeutic_analysis" where "enrolled_subjects" = 0
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the record should be included in all counts
    And "avg_enrolled_subjects" should include zero values in the average calculation

  # Validation: Large number of studies and subjects
  Scenario: Large dataset aggregation
    Given "study_therapeutic_analysis" contains 10,000 records across 50 therapeutic areas
    When the aggregation logic is executed
    Then the output should include 50 rows, one per therapeutic area
    And all aggregations should be accurate and performant

